  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-07, PR #835 (CI green before this note; merged immediately\nafter). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the item's own filed repro re-run on the shipped\nCLI -- five arms, one 2-file repository, one claim, one catalogue file,\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/busis_suppression_09072026/keyrepro/:\n\n  arm                                    BEFORE                    AFTER\n  extra_catalogs: {sources: [ok.yaml]}   violated, rc 1            violated, rc 1\n  extra_catalogs: {taint_sources: [..]}  confirmed_w_caveats, rc 3 Error, rc 2\n  extra_catalogs: {sources: <scalar>}    confirmed_w_caveats, rc 3 Error, rc 2\n  extra_catalogs: {sources: [{path:..}]} confirmed_w_caveats, rc 3 Error, rc 2\n  correct key, path does not exist       Error, rc 2               Error, rc 2\n\nAll three false all-clears are closed and BOTH controls are unchanged -- the\ncorrect declaration still finds the flow, and the pre-existing missing-path\nerror still fires. The typo arm's message carries the difflib hint the other\nallowlists already produce: \"unknown extra_catalogs field(s): 'taint_sources'\n(allowed: io_primitives, sanitizers, sinks, sources). Did you mean: sources?\"\n\nTHE FIX IS AT `load_claims`, not at `load_extra_catalog_paths`. That is where\nthe other four allowlists run, and `cli.py` calls it BEFORE the loader on the\nsame file. The loader stays lenient and its two leniency tests are untouched:\nits docstring already delegated the hard failure to a caller (\"the CLI layer\ndecides whether to fail hard; parsing is lenient\") and no caller existed. This\nis that caller. A parity test pins the allowlist against the keys the loader\nactually reads, so a key added to one and not the other cannot pass.\n\nRESIDUAL, FILED HERE RATHER THAN CHASED: the `verify-claims --help` text still\nintroduces this block by naming the FLAGS and never the sub-keys, which is what\nmakes `taint_sources:` the predictable typo. The gate now catches it with a\nhint, so the documentation gap is degraded from a false all-clear to a\ncorrectable error; naming the sub-keys in the help text would remove it."  # 90dc
